IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `iana-types`

-- Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK) — GOAL 1: EMPLOYMENT
-- CONTRARY TO s 15 (ss 15(1), 21(1B), 24, 25).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2006-13.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — employment contrary to s 15`

-- s 25(a) "“adult” means a person who has attained the age of 16". The
-- employee is an adult during the employment if their 16th birthday falls on
-- or before its last day.
@ref s 25(a)
GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is an adult during the employment in` e IF
    `add years` (e's `employee's date of birth`) 16 AT MOST e's `employed until`

-- s 15(1) "(a) he has not been granted leave to enter or remain in the United
-- Kingdom, or (b) his leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom— (i) is
-- invalid, (ii) has ceased to have effect ..., or (iii) is subject to a
-- condition preventing him from accepting the employment." s 24: a person on
-- immigration bail is treated as granted leave, and a restriction as to
-- employment as a condition of leave. s 21(1B) uses the same words.
@ref ss 15(1), 21(1B), 24
GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee's immigration status disqualifies them in` e IF
    CONSIDER e's `immigration position`
    WHEN `not subject to immigration control` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `leave permitting this employment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `immigration bail without such a restriction` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 15(1) "It is contrary to this section to employ an adult subject to
-- immigration control if" (a) or (b). s 25(b): employment under a contract
-- of service or apprenticeship.
@ref ss 15(1), 24, 25
@export Whether employing a person is contrary to s 15 of the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK): employment under a contract of service or apprenticeship of an adult (16 or over) subject to immigration control with no leave, or leave that is invalid, has ceased, or is subject to a condition preventing the employment (immigration bail counts as leave, and its employment restriction as a condition, s 24). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`  @desc The employee's date of birth, the dates of the employment, the contract, and the employee's immigration position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` e IF
        e's `under a contract of service or apprenticeship`
    AND `the employee is an adult during the employment in` e
    AND `the employee's immigration status disqualifies them in` e
